    {
      "id": "eddb123960f78a9ee2faf30cdf9d1943354a40cc",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 856319490,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "If we drop support for `-G` by itself, rather than `-G` with an argument, we can drop this requirement, by dropping the special-case handling of `-G`.  That would break compatibility with scripts that run `tshark -G` with no other arguments; is that an issue, or would that be sufficiently rare that we can just let it break?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-02-27T06:43:04.919Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-02-27T15:32:36.703Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 91964278,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2380,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 856423316,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "(There has been some discussion of moving forward (\"breaking things\") in 4.0: #17959)  \n  \n`-G fields` has been present for almost 20 years. Even though they weren't prodded, there has been plenty of time to update scripts that were using just `-G`.  \n\ne390d7e0 - Make the \"-G\" flag take an argument.  \n'... the argument to the \"-G\" flag; if no argument is specified,\n     for backwards compatibility we dump out a glossary of display\n     filter symbols.'\n  \n(In the beginning there were no arguments passed with `-G`)  \n[tethereal.c](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/b799cb10d931ee85eea1392178ff2a589199414c/tethereal.c#L156) \nAdd \"tethereal\", a tty-oriented derivative of Ethereal that works like Sun's snoop or like tcpdump.  \n```\n  /* If invoked with the \"-G\" flag, we dump out a glossary of\n     display filter symbols.\n\n     We do this here to mirror what happens in the GTK+ version, although\n     it's not necessary here. */\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-02-27T15:32:36.588Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-02-27T15:32:36.588Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 91964278,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2380,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
